// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// ANALYSIS OF ATTEMPT 20 REGRESSION (44.9% accuracy, 87.8% syntax vs. best 49.0%, 89.8%):
//
// ROOT CAUSE: `observedSpanThreshold = prefixBudget = 800` prevented entering constrained
// mode when the model wrote "<<" before step 800. This caused the model's natural
// "<<int({n} * {frac_1} * {frac_2})>>" spans to be written entirely in free text,
// with curly braces and "**" passing through unchecked (mode_D/E: 3 invalid spans).
// In the BEST (18), any "<<" triggers constrained mode, so the parser prevents `{n}`.
//
// THREE PRIMARY FIXES:
// 1. REMOVE observedSpanThreshold: Always enter constrained mode when "<<" is detected
//    (restoring best-18 behavior). The parser will then prevent `{n}`, `**`, etc.
//    This converts the 3 invalid-syntax spans to valid ones, and may fix 1-2 semantically
//    because the parser forces `n` instead of `{n}` which exactly matches correct answer.
//
// 2. FIX DELIMITER DETECTION: Replace exact `next == "<<"` check with
//    `RenderedEndsWith(generated, "<<")` after appending next. This is required by the
//    instructions and correctly handles space-prefixed tokens like " <<"
//    (e.g., Qwen3.5-9B may tokenize "<<" as a single token or split it).
//
// 3. MAINTAIN ALL OTHER PARAMETERS FROM BEST (18):
//    - prefixBudget = maxSteps - 100 = 800
//    - maxSpanTokens = 22
//    - nearBudgetThreshold = 30
//    - penaltyTokens = ["{", "}", "**", "^", "\\"]
//    - break after clean constrained span close (output ends at first constrained span)
//    - CloseSpanWithinBudget uses ALL remaining budget when triggered
//    - EOS inside span → CloseSpanWithinBudget with all remaining budget
//
// DESIGN RATIONALE FOR BREAK-AFTER-CLOSE:
// When we break after the first constrained span closes, the generated output ENDS
// at that close delimiter. So the evaluator's "last visible span" IS the constrained
// span we controlled. This is intentional: no subsequent unconstrained spans can
// override our controlled output.
//
// EXPECTED IMPROVEMENT:
// - mode_D/E (3 invalid spans): parser prevents {n} → valid syntax (+3 examples syntax)
// - One of those examples (juggler problem) has correct formula n*frac_1*frac_2 which
//   the parser produces when {n} → n → directly matches correct answer (+1 accuracy)
// - No regression from best (18) on other cases since structure is identical
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

